    "geometry_quality": "Real-traced from OSM route relation 1737997 (member ways chained with no gaps), cut at the North Hanley and 5th & Missouri station nodes: 13.70 mi against 13.9 mi documented for this stage. Draws today’s alignment, and only the stage opened in its first year.",
    "segments": [
     {
      "start": 1993,
      "end": 2026,
      "headway_min": 15,
      "note": "First section of MetroLink, opened 31 July 1993 from North Hanley through downtown St. Louis and across the Eads Bridge to 5th & Missouri in East St. Louis, Illinois. East Riverfront was added 14 May 1994 and Cortex 31 July 2018. Called the Lambert Airport branch until the lines were renamed Red and Blue on 27 October 2008. Headway is an estimate: Wikipedia gives 10–20 minutes for the system today, and no historic timetable was checked. A flash flood on 26 July 2022 shut the system for nearly 72 hours; that is shorter than the map can show, so the segment runs through it. Blue Line trains also use this track from Forest Park–DeBaliviere east; it is drawn once, under the Red Line, so the legend does not count it twice.",
      "sources": [
       "Segment-level: opening years from Wikipedia’s MetroLink chronology and station list. End year: still running in October 2026 reporting on the MidAmerica extension. Headway not checked against a timetable.",
